Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:38:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Write compressed NBT files in a single synced write

NbtIo.writeCompressed(tag, path) opened the file with SYNC and wrapped it in an 8 KB buffer, so every 8 KB of compressed output was a separate synchronous write. A 35 KB player file took five of them, about 47 ms on a virtual disk. Compress into memory first and write the result with one synced write, keeping the same durability. A failure while serialising also no longer truncates the existing file.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/nbt/NbtIo.java b/net/minecraft/nbt/NbtIo.java
index a4c411730c605920e79af2b9b9b6482de542caef..c694693cc55b5b8b4818eb69b3f4af828504e428 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/nbt/NbtIo.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/nbt/NbtIo.java
@@ -77,12 +77,13 @@ public class NbtIo {
     }
 
     public static void writeCompressed(final CompoundTag tag, final Path file) throws IOException {
-        try (
-            OutputStream out = Files.newOutputStream(file, SYNC_OUTPUT_OPTIONS);
-            OutputStream bufferedOut = new BufferedOutputStream(out);
-        ) {
-            writeCompressed(tag, bufferedOut);
+        // Misteln start - write compressed NBT files in a single synced write
+        java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream bytes = new java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream(64 * 1024);
+        writeCompressed(tag, bytes);
+        try (OutputStream out = Files.newOutputStream(file, SYNC_OUTPUT_OPTIONS)) {
+            bytes.writeTo(out);
         }
+        // Misteln end - write compressed NBT files in a single synced write
     }
 
     public static void writeCompressed(final CompoundTag tag, final OutputStream out) throws IOException {
